---
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import WhatsAppFloat from "../components/WhatsAppFloat.astro";
import { SITE } from "../consts";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const updated = "24 October 2026";
---

<Base
  title={`Privacy policy | ${SITE.brand}`}
  description="What www.medbrains.in collects, why, who it is shared with, how long it is kept, and how to exercise your rights under the DPDP Act."
>
  <Header />
  <main id="main" class="policy">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy policy</p>
      <h1>Privacy on this website</h1>
      <p class="meta">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <p>
        This policy covers www.medbrains.in, the MedBrains company website. It
        explains what we collect when you visit, why, and what you can do about
        it. It does not cover the MedBrains hospital software: patient records
        in that software belong to the hospital that uses it, and the hospital
        decides how they are used. We process them only on the hospital's
        instructions, under our contract with it.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>What you send us.</strong> If you use the demo form or write to
          us, we receive your name, phone number or email, your hospital's name
          and your message. The form opens a WhatsApp chat with your message
          filled in, so it reaches us through WhatsApp.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Usage analytics, only if you allow it.</strong> If you choose
          "Allow" on the analytics banner, Microsoft Clarity records how pages
          are used: clicks, scrolling and the pages visited. Form fields are
          masked. If you choose "No thanks", or make no choice, Clarity does not
          load. You can change your choice at any time with "Analytics choice"
          at the foot of every page.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Technical data.</strong> Like any website, our hosting
          (Amazon Web Services) receives your IP address and browser details
          when pages load. Our fonts are served from our own site, so no font
          service sees your visit.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not run advertising trackers, and we do not sell personal data.</p>

      <h2>Why we use it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To reply to you, arrange a demo and follow up on your enquiry.</li>
        <li>With your consent, to understand which pages help visitors and which confuse them.</li>
        <li>To keep the website running and secure.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who it is shared with</h2>
      <p>
        Only the services that run this website for us: Amazon Web Services
        (hosting), Microsoft (Clarity, only with your consent)
        and Meta (WhatsApp, when you message us). Each processes the data under
        its own terms. We share personal data with others only if the law
        requires it.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Enquiries are kept for as long as we are in conversation with you and
        for a reasonable period after, then deleted, unless a law requires us to
        keep them longer. You can ask us to delete yours sooner.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 you can ask us
        what personal data we hold about you, correct or update it, have it
        erased, withdraw consent you have given, and nominate someone to act
        for you. You can also raise a grievance with us. Write to
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>; we will reply within
        90 days, and usually much sooner. If you are not satisfied with our
        answer, you can complain to the Data Protection Board of India.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If we change this policy we will update the date at the top of this
        page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
  <WhatsAppFloat />
</Base>

<style>
  .policy { padding: 120px 0 96px; }
  .policy .wrap { max-width: 760px; }
  .policy h1 { margin: 8px 0 4px; }
  .policy h2 { margin: 40px 0 12px; font-size: 1.4rem; }
  .policy .meta { color: var(--night-text); margin-bottom: 32px; }
  .policy p, .policy li { line-height: 1.65; }
  .policy ul { padding-left: 1.2em; display: grid; gap: 10px; }
</style>
